    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0622" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.48/521</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Elkus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-18T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3280. Your 2387, January 8. Red Cross and Committee for Syrian Relief state that
                    Djemal Pasha’s request would largely divert relief supplies from original
                    purposes for which funds were solicited. If possible have all supplies landed
                    and distributed at Beirut. Only if absolutely necessary concession may be made
                    to have one-fourth landed at Jaffa, on condition that Philip<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d657-f1"/> and Red Cross representatives from Beirut proceed to
                    Jaffa and supervise distribution there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d657-f1" n="3" xml:id="d657-f1-content">
                <p> Hoffman Philip, Counselor of the Embassy at Constantinople.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
